WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:07.790
Hello, everyone!
Let's begin the June class of Kyoto Prosumer College.

2
00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:14.130
Speaking of June, it's umeboshi season.
The rainy season has just started, and our bodies can feel heavy and tired.

3
00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:23.390
I really recommend making umeboshi by hand every year at this time,
to help you get through the rainy season.

4
00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:26.630
is the biggest key to keeping umeboshi from molding.

5
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:29.070
To keep air out,

6
00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:30.870
a glass jar

7
00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:32.930
is very hard for air to get into,

8
00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:34.730
so I recommend it.

9
00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:36.110
Because air doesn't get in easily,

10
00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:37.750
even if you lower the salt,

11
00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.790
it's harder for mold to form.

12
00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:46.390
You can see the umezu has risen like this.

13
00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:50.170
This umezu is really delicious.

14
00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:55.970
It's so good, so please set some aside.

15
00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:58.890
It's such a beautiful red.

16
00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:04.170
The fresher the shiso, the more vivid this red is.

17
00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:09.770
Let's move on to the lecture.

18
00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:14.770
This is the ume work edition of the "Bringing Fermented Food Back to the Kitchen" series.

